From 114299bc52908781660ca87a01080fb1de016591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:53:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 54/69] input: drain the output when the end pauses instead of
 repeating

Pausing at the end takes priority over repeating it, so an item asked for
with both --play-and-pause and a repeat pauses at every end and never
repeats. Reaching the end does not drain the output on the way in, because
the repeat that was expected would have carried straight on and a drain
stops the output; the pause path then leaves the main loop without draining
it either, so the tail the output was still holding when the end was
noticed - a quarter of a second of it, since the repeat is given a cushion
to restart in - is dropped when the input is torn down.

Drain there too. A repeat that does not happen makes it an end like any
other, which is what the other way out of the loop already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/input.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/input.c b/src/input/input.c
index e825ccc8a0..d7e3fc619c 100644
--- a/src/input/input.c
+++ b/src/input/input.c
@@ -829,7 +829,13 @@ static void MainLoop( input_thread_t *p_input, bool b_interactive )
             else if( b_pause_after_eof && input_priv(p_input)->b_can_pause )
             {
                 if( b_paused_at_eof )
+                {
+                    /* Pausing at the end takes priority over repeating, so
+                     * reaching here is an end: drain what was left undrained
+                     * above. */
+                    es_out_Eos( input_priv(p_input)->p_es_out );
                     break;
+                }
 
                 vlc_value_t val = { .i_int = PAUSE_S };
 
